  "description": "Dean's proposal, 2026-08-09: drop the top of the cost curve instead of adding an upgrade rule. Tier 1 costs 1-2 cards, Tier 2 costs 2-3, Tier 3 costs 3-4, and nothing in the game costs 5 or 6. Every Tier 2 and Tier 3 card is 3-of-suit plus wilds today, so the suit gate is left alone as the tier signature and the WILD component is what comes off: T2 3+0 -> 2+0 and 3+1 -> 3+0, T3 3+2 -> 3+0 and 3+3 -> 3+1. A6 The Garden Hive, the one 3-cost Tier 1, comes to 2. A PRICE arm, not a power arm: it tests whether affordability alone gets the upper tiers into play, and whether anything else moves when it does.",
